The sysupgrade.bin image is reported to be OEM web flashed with an ncc_att_hwid appended.  ncc_att_hwid is a 32bit binary in the GPL Source download for either the TEW-810DR or DIR-810L and is located at source/user/wolf/cameo/ncc/hostTools.

The invocation is: ''ncc_att_hwid -f tew-810dr-squashfs-factory.bin -a -m "TEW-810DR" -H "1.0R" -r "WW" -c "1.0"''

This may need to be altered if your hardware version is "1.1R".

==== TFTP + serial installation ====

  - Load ''*.sysupgrade.bin'' to your tftp server directory and rename for convenience.
  - Set a static ip 192.168.10.100.
  - NIC cable to a lan port.
  - Serial connection parameters 57600,8N1
  - Power on the TEW-810DR and press 4 for a U-Boot command line prompt.
  - Verify IP's with U-Boot command ''printenv''.
  - Adjust tftp settings if needed per the tftp documentation
  - Boot the tftp image to test the build.
  - If the image loads, reset your server ip to 192.168.1.10 and restart network.
  - Log in to Luci, 192.168.1.1, and flash the ''*sysupgrade.bin'' image.


